I go back towards the office.
On the way, I see a fruit cart.
There are many fresh fruits on the cart.
I see yellow bananas on the cart.
I stop near the cart.
The fruit seller is standing there.
"Dada, how much are a dozen bananas for?" I ask.
"Madam, sixty rupees for a dozen," he says.
"Give me half a dozen bananas," I tell him.
The fruit seller takes six bananas.
He puts those bananas in a paper bag.
He gives that bag to me.
I take my wallet out of my bag.
I give him thirty rupees.
He takes the money.
I put the bag of bananas safely in my bag.
I go back inside the office.
